<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parakramabahu II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">reigned <a href="/years/1236">1236</a>–<a href="/years/1270">1270</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Parakramabahu II was king of Dambadeniya in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> from 1236 to 1270, the most celebrated ruler of that dynasty. He drove the forces of the invader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinga-magha">Magha</a> out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polonnaruwa">Polonnaruwa</a>, held a coronation there and convened a council to reform the Buddhist monastic order. A learned king, he is credited with the Sinhala poem Kavsilumina.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/parakramabahu-ii.jpg" alt="Parakramabahu II" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mr Jean-Michel Moullec · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Parakramabahu_II_-_Massa_Photo_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
